 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
--   **Precision:** Hash collisions in the grid may affect color accuracy [S1].
--   **Boundaries:** Pruning too aggressively may remove essential Gaussians, leading to holes in the scene [S1, S2].
--   **Degenerate Input:** If the scene has high-frequency details, a small codebook may not capture the geometric diversity, leading to artifacts [S1].
+*   **Sparse Scenes:** The grid-based color representation may struggle in sparse settings where neighboring Gaussians are far apart, as spatial redundancy is lower [S1, S2].
+*   **High-Frequency Details:** Pruning may remove Gaussians contributing to fine details if the mask regularization is too aggressive [S2].
 
